Background. An (n+1)-colored graph is a pair (Γ, γ) where Γ is a finite multigraph (loops not allowed) that is (n+1)-regular, and γ : E(Γ) → {0,1,…,n} is an edge-coloring such that edges incident to a common vertex receive pairwise distinct colors. From such a graph one builds an n-dimensional simplicial pseudocomplex K(Γ), the colored-graph polyhedron, by taking an n-simplex σ(v) for each vertex v of Γ with vertices labeled 0,…,n, and gluing σ(v) to σ(w) along their codimension-1 faces opposite the vertex labeled c whenever v and w are joined by an edge of color c, matching corresponding labels. The graph (Γ, γ) is said to represent a closed piecewise-linear (PL) n-manifold M if |K(Γ)| is PL homeomorphic to M.

Problem. For n = 4, give purely combinatorial / algebraic graph-theoretic characterizations describing exactly which 5-colored graphs represent closed PL 4-manifolds whose fundamental group belongs to each of the following classes:
(a) finite groups;
(b) free products of groups;
(c) surface groups (i.e., fundamental groups of closed surfaces);
(d) poly-(finite or cyclic) groups;
(e) amenable groups.

Equivalently, for each class C above, describe by intrinsic graph-theoretic conditions on (Γ, γ) the family of 5-colored graphs (Γ, γ) representing closed PL 4-manifolds M with π₁(M) ∈ C.

